  "notes": [
    "Contactor terminals labeled 11/21 (line pole) and 23/23 (second pole) per drawing; coil terminals A1/A2 are assigned designations — the diagram shows the coil but does not print terminal numbers.",
    "Start components *ST (thermistor), *SC (start capacitor), *SR (start relay) internal terminal numbering partly inferred from SR block (1,2,5); Note #8 governs this assembly and some spade assignments were ambiguous.",
    "The 24-volt control path between the LPS/DTS/HPS/CTD string and the indoor blower/thermostat loop uses dashed field-wiring in the source; exact node merges around the blower-motor relay block and EXTERNAL POWER SUPPLY 24V (Note #3) transformer were partly ambiguous and traced conservatively.",
    "CAP terminal letters read as H (herm/start), C (common), F (fan). Wire colors BLU/YEL/BRN taken from printed labels.",
    "*LLS shown twice (upper-right schematic and lower connection area); treated as one liquid-line solenoid device.",
    "Right-hand SCHEMATIC DIAGRAM portion is cropped at page edge; only the CONNECTION DIAGRAM was traced for structure.",
    "Notes #13, #14 callouts referenced on drawing but note text not legible in this crop."
  ]
}